 "read_this_first": "Every program that is the buggy one with one piece taken out, some 40 candidates a bug and no lesson behind any of them, repairs 19 of the 100 scored HumanEvalFix bugs; 15 of the repairs are right as far as checked and 4 pass the tests without being right. Of the 19 bugs that are something too much it repairs 11 (10 right); the learner with 2,864 lessons repairs 8 of them. Put in front of the learner within the same 200 candidates the two repair 58 against the learner's 55 and are right for 49 against 48: four bugs won that the learner did not repair, two right repairs lost to a piece that passes weak tests first, one pushed out of the 200. So it adds three repairs and one right answer. That is less than was written down beforehand: five of the seven statements of the expectation did not hold, though neither of the two that would have made me drop it came true. Of the 22 bugs nothing without a model had repaired it repairs one. One run, one machine, by the producer; nobody else has re-run it.",
