 "what_this_does_not_show": [
  "Not that deleting code repairs real bugs. HumanEvalFix bugs that are something too much were made by adding a piece to a correct program, so the piece taken out is the fix by construction. In real projects such bugs are a small share, and since Kali (ISSTA 2015) it is known that deletion mostly makes weak tests pass.",
  "Not a gain in right answers worth the name: 49 against 48 is one bug in one run.",
  "The 22 were known by type before the family was built (7 of them something too much). That is why the family was looked for; it was shaped on the development bugs only, and the scored bugs were run once.",
  "Right as far as checked means: the published fix, or the same answers as the published fix on the extra inputs of HumanEval+ Mini. It is not a proof.",
  "The learner was not run again beside the pieces; the sum is arithmetic on its recorded places. A piece that is also among the learner's first candidates is counted twice against the budget, which can only make the sum smaller.",
